/// Behavioral API documentation for the ICP Portal backend. Static Markdown
/// authored from the current backend source; it reads no runtime state.
mixin () {
  public query func getApiDoc() : async Text {
    "# ICP Portal Backend API\n\n## Purpose\n\nThe ICP Portal backend is the per-user workspace store for the ICP Portal application shell. It persists each user's home-screen layout (installed apps, personal shortcuts, folders, dock), the curated ICP application registry, file and folder metadata, notes and note folders, calculator history, application settings, and a workspace-wide bug-report inbox. Every per-user record is owned by the Internet Identity principal that created it and is never visible to another principal; bug reports are workspace-wide and readable only by the workspace admin.\n\n## Authentication\n\nEvery workspace endpoint requires a signed-in, non-anonymous caller. Anonymous callers are rejected with a trap: `Sign in required`. There is no anonymous read path.\n\nThe frontend pins an Internet Identity derivation origin, published at `/.well-known/ii-derivation-origin` when available. An agent already holding the user's Internet Identity authorization derives the correct per-app principal against that origin (for example `icp identity link web <name> --app <host>`). Such a delegation acts with the user's full authority in this app until it expires.\n\n## Authorization and identity\n\nWorkspace endpoints have no role gate: authorization is per-principal ownership. Each caller reads and writes only its own state, keyed by the caller principal. A principal that has never signed in through the app's own frontend has no stored state; read endpoints return empty results and write endpoints create a fresh empty state for that principal on first use. A signed-in caller derived against a different origin is a different principal than the one the frontend registered, and therefore sees a different (empty) workspace.\n\nThe bug-report endpoints are the exception. `submitBugReport` is open to any signed-in caller and captures the reporter principal server-side. `listBugReports`, `getBugReport`, `setBugReportStatus` and `setBugReportAiResult` are admin-only: a non-admin caller traps with `Unauthorized: Only the workspace admin can view or manage reports`. The workspace admin is the principal holding the `#admin` role in the shared authorization state; the first caller to initialize access control receives the admin role.\n\nThe shared authorization mixin (`MixinAuthorization`) is included for platform role management; the workspace endpoints themselves do not consult roles.\n\n## Units and encoding\n\n- Timestamps (`createdAt`, `updatedAt`, `installedAt`) are signed nanosecond `Int` values from `Time.now()`.\n- Identifiers (`id`, `appId`, `folderId`, `parentId`) are `Nat` counters, unique per principal (and workspace-wide for report ids).\n- `FileRef.blob` is an off-chain object-storage blob handle; `sizeBytes` and `mimeType` are optional.\n- `StorageSection` is the variant `#local` or `#icpCloud`.\n- `LaunchType` is `#native`, `#icpService`, `#externalWeb` or `#comingSoon`.\n- `AppCategory` is one of `#ai`, `#finance`, `#social`, `#productivity`, `#governance`, `#gaming`, `#media`, `#developer`, `#business`, `#other`.\n- `HomeItem` is the variant `#app(InstalledApp)` or `#folder(HomeFolder)`.\n- `ReportStatus` is `#open`, `#inProgress`, `#resolved` or `#closed`; a new report starts `#open`.\n- `BugReport.category` and `BugReport.summary` are optional AI results; `null` means no AI assistance was applied.\n- `UserSettings.wallpaper` names the active wallpaper image; `UserSettings.wallpaperEnabled` is the per-principal on/off toggle for that wallpaper. `getSettings` returns `wallpaperEnabled = true` by default, and `updateSettings` persists the caller's chosen value.\n\n## Shortcuts and website links\n\nPersonal shortcuts are per-principal and stored alongside installed apps. `createShortcut`, `renameShortcut`, `setShortcutIcon`, `setShortcutUrl`, `setShortcutFavourite`, `moveShortcutToFolder` and `removeShortcut` manage them; `listShortcuts` reads them. A shortcut can be favourited and moved into a home folder exactly like an installed app.\n\nEvery shortcut address is validated before it is stored. `createShortcut` and `setShortcutUrl` reject an unusable address by trapping with a clear, user-facing message: `Enter a web address, for example https://example.com` (empty), `Address must start with http:// or https://` (missing or non-web scheme), `Address is missing a website name` (empty host), or `Address cannot contain spaces`. Only absolute `http://` and `https://` addresses with a non-empty host are accepted; an invalid address is never stored.\n\n## Directory and Explore ICP\n\nThe ICP App Directory is a curated, categorised catalogue of ICP ecosystem apps, browsable with `listDirectory` (optional category filter) and searchable with `searchDirectory` (case-insensitive name or description match). Each entry reports its availability: `#installed` (on the caller's home screen), `#available`, or `#comingSoon`. `#comingSoon` entries are labelled and never launch. `addToHomeScreen` installs an available entry; `setDirectoryFavourite` favourites it (installing it first when needed). The catalogue includes verified ICP wallets, explorers, developer tools and community apps, with corrected URLs for MULTI/DEX (`https://multidex.ai`) and Caffeine (`https://caffeine.ai`), and Internet Identity pointing at its current official address (`https://id.ai`).\n\nA fresh workspace is seeded with a real, editable home folder named `Explore ICP` containing shortcuts to DFINITY (`https://dfinity.org`), Internet Computer (`https://internetcomputer.org`), OpenCloud (`https://opencloud.org`) and ICP Skills (`https://skills.internetcomputer.org`). The folder can be renamed, its shortcuts edited or removed, and apps moved in or out like any other folder.\n\n## Settings\n\n`getSettings` returns the caller's per-principal application settings: `theme`, `wallpaper`, `wallpaperEnabled`, `gridSize`, `reduceMotion` and `updatedAt`. Defaults for a principal with no stored settings are `theme = \"system\"`, `wallpaper = \"default\"`, `wallpaperEnabled = true`, `gridSize = 4`, `reduceMotion = false` and `updatedAt = 0`. `updateSettings` replaces the whole settings record for the signed-in caller and stamps `updatedAt` with the current time; it returns the stored record. The wallpaper on/off toggle is `wallpaperEnabled`: when `false` the frontend hides the wallpaper image while keeping the chosen `wallpaper` value.\n\n## Lifecycle and polling\n\nAll endpoints are synchronous request/response; there is no job to poll. Read endpoints (`listAppRegistry`, `getAppRegistryEntry`, `listInstalledApps`, `listHomeItems`, `getDock`, `listShortcuts`, `listFolder`, `searchFiles`, `sortFolder`, `getNote`, `listNotes`, `searchNotes`, `listNoteFolders`, `listCalcHistory`, `getSettings`, `listDirectory`, `searchDirectory`, `getDirectoryEntry`, `listFavourites`, `listBugReports`, `getBugReport`) are `query` calls and return the current state immediately. Write endpoints are update calls and return the resulting record.\n\n## Mutation retry safety\n\nWrite endpoints are not idempotent in general. `installApp`, `createHomeFolder`, `createShortcut`, `createFolder`, `addFile`, `copyFile`, `createNote`, `createNoteFolder`, `addCalcEntry` and `submitBugReport` allocate a new id on every call, so retrying a call that actually succeeded creates a duplicate. `rename*`, `move*`, `set*`, `update*` and `delete*` are idempotent in effect: repeating them converges on the same state. `deleteFolder` (files) removes the folder and its entire subtree; `deleteHomeFolder` returns its apps to the home screen; `deleteNoteFolder` unfiles its notes. `clearCalcHistory` is destructive and irreversible.\n\n## Errors and gotchas\n\n- Anonymous callers trap with `Sign in required` on every workspace endpoint.\n- Non-admin callers trap with `Unauthorized: Only the workspace admin can view or manage reports` on the bug-report inbox endpoints.\n- An invalid shortcut address traps with the validation message described above; the address is never stored.\n- Endpoints that target a missing record return `null` (optionals) or `false` (booleans) rather than trapping.\n- `installApp` returns `null` when the app is not registered or is already installed.\n- `moveAppToFolder` and `moveShortcutToFolder` return `null` when the target record or folder does not exist.\n- `moveFolder` refuses to move a folder into itself or one of its descendants and returns `null`.\n- The application registry is seeded per principal on first use and is identical for every user; it is read-only through the API.\n- The OQL `schema()` and `execute()` endpoints expose the workspace tables to the Caffeine Data Intelligence agent; per-user tables are scoped to the caller's own rows, and the bug-report table is controller-only.\n";
  };
};
